 A binary distribution also carries third-party components, which the stanzas
 below carve out. Which ones are actually inside any given package is derived at
 release time rather than declared: packaging/collect-notices.py writes the
 manifest share/doc/pist/THIRD-PARTY.txt from the artifact's real contents, and
 every licence text into share/doc/pist/licenses/. The file patterns here are
 written to match whichever layout the package uses — the Linux .deb and .rpm
 keep the bundle in the private prefix /usr/lib/pist, the AppImage and the plain
 archives use usr/ or bin/ beside the executable, and the macOS bundle uses
 pist.app/Contents/. share/doc/pist/NOTICE is the authoritative prose account.

