# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The system libraries a self-contained bundle carries, and the licence texts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files: */lib/*.so.* */bin/*.dll
Copyright: the respective projects
License: bundled-library
Comment:
 Libraries a bundle picks up because Qt and SDL2 link them — the X, audio, TLS
 and glib stack. They are unmodified copies of what the build host provided, and
 none of them is part of PiST. The components named by a stanza above (Qt, SDL2,
 libpng, zlib, Capstone) are more specific and take precedence for their own
 files; this one is the catch-all for the rest.

Files: */licenses/distro/*
Copyright: the respective projects
License: bundled-library
Comment:
 The build host's own copyright file for each of the libraries above, as
 linuxdeploy copied it. In the .deb and .rpm they live here rather than in
 /usr/share/doc/<package>/, where dpkg knows them to belong to another package
 and refuses to let this one take them.

